<fields id="fieldset_0" length="64">
  <text_before_fields><para>This register reports information about the candidate HPPI for the VPE selected by <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_vpe_selr.xml" state="">IRS_VPE_SELR</register_link>.</para>
<para>This register is updated after a write that sets <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_vpe_selr.xml" state="">IRS_VPE_SELR</register_link>.S to 1 when <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_vpe_statusr.xml" state="">IRS_VPE_STATUSR</register_link>.{V, IDLE} is {1, 1}.</para>
<para>If there is a change in the HPPI for the VPE following the write that sets <register_link id="irs_config_frame.irs_vpe_selr.xml" state="">IRS_VPE_SELR</register_link>.S to 1, it is <arm-defined-word>IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED</arm-defined-word> whether the old or the new HPPI is reported in this register.</para></text_before_fields>
  <field id="fieldset_0-63_33" has_partial_fieldset="False" is_linked_to_partial_fieldset="False" is_access_restriction_possible="False" is_variable_length="False" is_constant_value="False" is_partial_field="False" is_conditional_field_name="False" rwtype="RES0">
    <field_msb>63</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>33</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>63:33</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before"/>
    <field_description order="before">
      <para>Reserved, <arm-defined-word>RES0</arm-defined-word>.</para>
    </field_description>
  </field>
  <field id="fieldset_0-32_32" has_partial_fieldset="False" is_linked_to_partial_fieldset="False" is_access_restriction_possible="False" is_variable_length="False" is_constant_value="False" is_partial_field="False" is_conditional_field_name="False">
    <field_name>HPPIV</field_name>
    <field_msb>32</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>32</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>32</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before">
      <para>Whether there is a candidate HPPI for the VPE.</para>
    </field_description>
    <field_description order="after">
      <para>When the value of this field is 1, ID and TYPE together form the INTID of the candidate HPPI for the VPE.</para>
    </field_description>
    <field_values impdef="False">
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b0</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>Invalid: There is no candidate HPPI for the VPE.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
      <field_value_instance>
        <field_value>0b1</field_value>
        <field_value_description>
          <para>VALID: There is a candidate HPPI for the VPE.</para>
        </field_value_description>
      </field_value_instance>
    </field_values>
  </field>
  <field id="fieldset_0-31_29" has_partial_fieldset="False" is_linked_to_partial_fieldset="False" is_access_restriction_possible="False" is_variable_length="False" is_constant_value="False" is_partial_field="False" is_conditional_field_name="False">
    <field_name>TYPE</field_name>
    <field_msb>31</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>29</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>31:29</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before"><para>The encoding of this field depends upon the value in HPPIV as described below:</para>
<list type="unordered">
<listitem><content>
<para>If HPPIV is 0, this field is <arm-defined-word>RES0</arm-defined-word>.</para>
</content>
</listitem><listitem><content>
<para>If HPPIV is 1, this field contains valid information.</para>
</content>
</listitem></list></field_description>
    <field_description order="after">
      <para>Values not defined above are reserved.</para>
    </field_description>
    <field_values impdef="False">
